# Build context is the repo root, but the Dockerfile only needs
# packages/backend. Without this, every build uploads the entire monorepo
# (web source + dist, mobile assets, node_modules) before COPY runs. On a
# starter plan with no cache that is slow and has already produced one failed
# auto-deploy.
#
# Docker's COPY ignores .gitignore, so node_modules and .env MUST be excluded
# explicitly here or they get baked into the image layer.

.git
.gitignore
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
*.err
.opencode

# Dependencies: reinstalled inside the image by npm install.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output: regenerated by npm run build.
dist
**/dist
build
**/build

# Not needed by the backend image.
packages/web
packages/mobile
packages/admin
docs
*.md
Dockerfile
.dockerignore